# {{ project_name }}

PySpark job deployed with a Databricks Asset Bundle on
{% if compute == 'serverless' %}serverless compute (environment {{ serverless_environment }}){% else %}a job cluster (DBR {{ databricks_runtime }} LTS){% endif %}, Python {{ runtime.python }}.

## Prerequisites

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- Java {{ runtime.java }} (local Spark for unit tests)
- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) authenticated on `{{ databricks_host }}`:
  `databricks auth login --host {{ databricks_host }}`

## Development loop

```bash
make install            # uv sync + pre-commit hooks
make test               # unit tests on local Spark + Delta (no workspace needed)
make test-integration   # integration tests on the workspace via Databricks Connect
make run-dev            # deploy your personal copy of the bundle and run the job
```

In dev, the job is named `[dev <you>] …`, its schedule is paused and it writes to
`{{ unity_catalog_name }}.dev_<you>`, so every developer has an isolated copy.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `databricks.yml` | Bundle: targets (dev / staging / prod) and their variables |
| `resources/` | Jobs deployed by the bundle |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/main.py` | Wheel entry point, receives `--catalog`, `--schema`, `--log-level` |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/jobs/` | Jobs wiring I/O and transformations |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/transformations/` | Pure DataFrame → DataFrame functions |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/io.py` | Unity Catalog / Delta readers and writers |
| `tests/unit/` | Local Spark tests |
| `tests/integration/` | Databricks Connect tests (read-only on the workspace) |

Add a job by creating a module in `jobs/` exposing `run(spark, cfg)` and registering it in `_JOBS` in `main.py`.

## Configuration

Settings that change per environment are bundle variables, set per target in `databricks.yml`
and passed to the job as parameters:

| Variable | dev | staging | prod |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `catalog` | `{{ unity_catalog_name }}` | `{{ unity_catalog_name }}` | `{{ unity_catalog_name }}` |
| `schema` | `dev_<you>` | `{{ package_name }}_staging` | `{{ package_name }}` |
| `log_level` | `DEBUG` | `INFO` | `INFO` |
| `pause_status` | `PAUSED` | `PAUSED` | `UNPAUSED` |

To add a setting: declare a variable in `databricks.yml`, pass it in `resources/{{ package_name }}_job.yml`,
then read it in `main.py`.

The deploying identity needs `USE CATALOG` and `CREATE SCHEMA` on `{{ unity_catalog_name }}`.

## Deployment

| Target | How |
| --- | --- |
| dev | `make run-dev` |
| staging | automatic on push to `main`: deploy, run the job, integration tests |
| prod | automatic on `v*` tag, gated by the `production` GitHub environment |

CI authenticates with a service principal (OAuth M2M): set `DATABRICKS_HOST`, `DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID`
and `DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET` in the `staging` and `production` GitHub environments.

## Updating from the template

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```
